WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.300
Hugo Weaving isn't one to be pushed around
even by Mighty Marvel.

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:08.160
The actor recently revealed that he passed
on the opportunity to reprise the role of

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:13.480
Red Skull in Avengers: Infinity War and Avengers:
Endgame when contract negotiations with Marvel

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.440
Studios hit a serious snag.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.960
Weaving spoke about the situation during an
interview with TimeOut to promote his appearance

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:24.320
in The Visit, a stage production being mounted
at London's famed National Theatre.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:28.560
The Skull's reappearance as keeper of the
Soul Stone on the planet Vormir was one of

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.190
the more unexpected and crowd-pleasing moments
in Infinity War, but to this day, there are

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:37.460
probably a number of fans who don't realize
that it wasn't Weaving under the makeup.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:41.629
Rather, it was Ross Marquand of The Walking
Dead fame who so thoroughly nailed Weaving's

00:00:41.629 --> 00:00:46.300
take on the character that audiences could
be forgiven for failing to spot the substitution.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:47.600
"I am prepared."

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.660
"We all think that at first.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.260
We are all wrong."

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:01.800
Surprisingly, Weaving indicated to TimeOut
that, in contrast to remarks he made in 2012

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.189
indicating that playing the Skull was, quote,
"not something [he] would want to do again,"

00:01:05.189 --> 00:01:09.391
he actually enjoyed the chance to indulge
his villainous impulses in the role, and would

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.160
have been down to return if only Marvel had
played ball.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:13.260
The actor explained:

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:16.360
"I loved playing that character Red Skull
it was a lot of fun.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:20.770
We were all obliged to sign up for three pictures:
I was thinking [Red Skull] probably wouldn't

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:24.940
come back in [another Captain America movie],
but he may well come back as a villain in

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:25.700
[an Avengers film]."

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:29.740
This turned out to be reasonably accurate,
although the Skull was more of a supporting

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:33.380
character than a villain in Infinity War and
Endgame so, what went wrong?

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:37.920
Weaving says that while he was indeed approached
to reprise the role, Marvel basically failed

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:42.340
to abide by the terms of the agreement that
was forged when he signed on for Captain America:

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:43.220
The First Avenger.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:44.160
Weaving claimed:

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:47.780
"They'd pushed back on the contracts that
we agreed on, and so the money they offered

00:01:47.789 --> 00:01:52.299
me [to return] was much less than I got for
the very first one, and this was for two films.

00:01:52.299 --> 00:01:56.270
And the promise when we first signed the contracts
was that the money would grow each time.

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:59.700
… I actually found negotiating with them
through my agent impossible.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.660
And I didn't really wanna do it that much.

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:02.660
But I would have done it."

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:08.660
"He resented my genius and tried to deny me
what was rightfully mine…"

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:13.900
Well, that's certainly a bummer to know but,
like we said, Marquand stepped in and absolutely

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.700
crushed the role in both movies.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:20.560
In fact, even though it's tough to envision
a circumstance in which the HYDRA mastermind-turned-Infinity

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:25.370
Stone guardian would make a return to the
MCU, Marquand has enthusiastically stated

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:28.180
that he would love to come back for another
go-round as the Skull.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:30.640
We have the feeling you're now asking a couple
of questions.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:34.460
"Wait a minute, Looper," you're asking, "Aren't
they making another Matrix movie?

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.820
Will we see Weaving in his signature role
of Agent Smith one more time?"

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:40.060
Yes, they are, and no, we won't.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:44.300
Hey, you've got questions, and we've got answers,
even if they're not exactly the ones you want.

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:48.620
Later in his TimeOut interview, Weaving explained
that he had indeed been offered the role of

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:54.210
Smith in director Lana Wachowski's upcoming,
as-yet untitled Matrix 4 but unfortunately,

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:56.340
the stars had stubbornly refused to align.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:57.340
Weaving dished:

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:59.220
"[Matrix 4] is a very different story.

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:03.220
It's unfortunate, but actually I had this
offer [for The Visit] and then the offer came

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:07.100
[for] The Matrix, so I knew it was happening,
but I didn't have dates.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:10.629
I thought [I] could do both, and it took eight
weeks to work out that the dates would work

00:03:10.629 --> 00:03:13.860
— I held off on accepting [his role in The
Visit for that period].

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:17.870
I was in touch with Lana Wachowski, but in
the end she decided that the dates weren't

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:18.580
going to work.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:21.940
So we'd sorted the dates, and then she sort
of changed her mind.

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:23.320
They're pushing on ahead without me."

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:27.840
That is also a bummer, as it either means
that Matrix 4 will be without Agent Smith

00:03:27.849 --> 00:03:31.959
altogether, or will have to fill the role
with someone other than Weaving, whose icy,

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:34.720
near-mechanical delivery helped define the
character.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:39.099
We can't help but wonder if Wachowski has
given Marquand a call; he does a pretty solid

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:40.420
Hugo Weaving impression.

